{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation (read-only, production MCP host i-00880b2c7f13527c5, 2026-11-05)\n\nThe production MCP tickets clone (`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, container label `rebar.service=mcp`) has received no git object maintenance since early September:\n\n- `git count-objects -v`: 74,605 loose objects (8.63 GiB loose), 235 packs (2.16 GiB), 306,528 commits.\n- `.git/objects/info/commit-graph` dated 2026-08-31; `objects/info/packs` dated 2026-09-02.\n- Local operator checkout of the same history: 6 packs, 333 MiB loose, current commit-graph chain.\n\nHistory walks there are much slower than on a clone of the same history:\n\n| walk (same command as rebar.attest.authorship_resolution) | production (shared clone in the container) | operator clone |\n|---|---|---|\n| store-wide `build_position_commit_map` (`-- '*.json'`) | 427.5 s | 111 s (bug breezelike-travelsick-moray, 2026-11-03 comment) |\n| per-ticket map, 26a0-0104-9b63-4500 | 160.8 s | 19.1 s |\n| per-ticket map, fb16-a8b0-c2b7-449a | 266.1 s | not measured |\n\nThe store-wide walk exceeds its 300 s timeout in production, so the compaction sweep's shared position map is always `None` there and every fold falls back to a per-ticket walk. Bug breezelike-travelsick-moray moves that walk outside the store write lock; it does not make the walk faster, so a production sweep still spends minutes per ticket before each fold.\n\nStore commits run with automatic maintenance disabled (`_AUTOMAINT_OFF` in compact.py and the commit seam), and `gc.autodetach=false`, `maintenance.autodetach=false` are set on the clone. Unverified: which component, if any, is meant to repack or rewrite the commit-graph on the production clone, and whether the 2 vCPU host or the 3.6 GiB container memory cap also contribute.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe production tickets clone's object store stays packed with a current commit-graph, so path-limited history walks cost about what they cost on a fresh clone, and the store-wide position walk finishes inside its timeout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The mechanism that should keep the production tickets clone packed (or its absence) is identified with evidence.\n- [x] [non-codebase] After the fix, production `git count-objects -v` shows loose objects bounded and the commit-graph current, measured read-only via SSM.\n  provenance: environment=production MCP host i-00880b2c7f13527c5, containers rebar-mcp-334295da063a-8092 and rebar-mcp-aa1e294069a5-8093 on the shared tickets clone; principal=AWS SSM RunCommand under the operator's frontier profile, executing as the instance role; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the measurement is a read-only git command run inside the live production container, so it only exists in production and cannot be reproduced from the repository.\n- [x] [non-codebase] The store-wide position walk completes inside its 300 s timeout in production, measured on a shared clone in the container.\n  provenance: environment=production MCP host i-00880b2c7f13527c5, container rebar-mcp-aa1e294069a5-8093 (release 0.15.1, contains the fix) on the shared tickets clone; principal=AWS SSM RunCommand under the operator's frontier profile, executing as the instance role; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the measurement is a read-only git command run inside the live production container, so it only exists in production and cannot be reproduced from the repository."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794442223483537565,"uuid":"49b778cc-c9ac-44e4-9e0d-5c4f07de215a"}